      "heading": "Part 1",
      "text": "So in this first lesson we're going to go over our fundamentals and of course the most  fundamental step is your basic steps.  So let's get right into it.  Make sure you're standing nice and straight, face your partner, take your partner's hand  and what we're going to do here is have the guy step back first since guys are leading  you're going to step back with your left foot.  One, step back with the right."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.34,
      "end": 63.54,
      "heading": "Part 2",
      "text": "Two, left foot in place.  Then from here you're going to go right foot forward, left foot forward, right foot in  place.  Ladies, you're just going to mirror your partner by stepping forward with your right,  forward the left, right in place, then left back, right back, left in place.  Let's do that a couple of times with the counts.  So here we go.  We're going to go one, two, three, five, six, seven, one, two, three, five, six, seven, one,"
    },
    {
      "start": 63.54,
      "end": 66.9,
      "heading": "Part 3",
      "text": "two, three, five, six, seven."
    },
    {
      "start": 83.54,
      "end": 135.34,
      "heading": "Part 4",
      "text": "All right.  So just one last tip about the basic.  So notice in the demo that typically when we step most of the weight is on our toes.  So yeah, let me get my shoes so that I can show you what I mean.  Okay.  So let's see.  Grab this.  Typically when we walk the motion is like this, your heel touches the ground first and  then the weight transfers onto your toe and then you kind of push it off into the next"
    },
    {
      "start": 135.34,
      "end": 159.7,
      "heading": "Part 5",
      "text": "step.  All right.  And salsa, it's pretty much the opposite.  You're going to start with your toe touching the ground and then gradually transfer the  weight down.  Okay.  And you're never going to fully put your weight on your heel.  Okay.  So even if your heel does touch the ground in which case maybe you're wearing high heels  like most of the ladies are going to be doing.  Okay.  Even if the heel touches, it's not going to be like you're putting your weight into it."
    },
    {
      "start": 159.7,
      "end": 183.48000000000002,
      "heading": "Part 6",
      "text": "Okay.  And the reason for that is because as you learn your trans, you're going to be spinning on  this part of your foot.  So you want to make sure that the weight is here so that you can easily and effectively spin.  Just remember that when you're practicing your basic and make sure you pass your basic  step before with the toes first, not the heel.  Okay.  So that pretty much wraps it up for the first lesson."
